THOUGHT: The parameter is explicitly annotated @Nullable, so dereferencing it directly causes the NullAway error. I should add a null check and define sensible behavior when color is null, without changing other methods. A reasonable choice is to reset this color to transparent black (0,0,0,0) when null is passed. After modifying the file, I’ll run the NullAway build to confirm the error count decreases by one and that no new errors are introduced.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/libgdx && sed -i '117,122c\  public Color set(@Nullable Color color) {
    if (color == null) {
      this.r = 0f;
      this.g = 0f;
      this.b = 0f;
      this.a = 0f;
    } else {
      this.r = color.r;
      this.g = color.g;
      this.b = color.b;
      this.a = color.a;
    }
    return this;
  }' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/graphics/Color.java && ./gradlew gdx:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -E "NullAway|error(s) found" -n new_build_output.log | tail
```

